{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":58971171,"ns":0,"title":"Adjustable pressure-limiting valve","extract":"An adjustable pressure-limiting valve (commonly abbreviated to APL valve, and also referred to as an expiratory valve, relief valve or spill valve) is a type of flow control valve used in anaesthesiology as part of a breathing system. It allows excess fresh gas flow and exhaled gases to leave the system while preventing ambient air from entering.","description":"Flow control valve used in anaesthesiology","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}